🚀 Full Stack .NET Developer Roadmap (From Scratch to Advanced)
1. Programming Foundations (Language-Agnostic, but C#/JavaScript preferred)

Basics of Programming

Input/Output, Variables & Data Types

Operators (Arithmetic, Relational, Logical, Bitwise)

Conditional Statements (if-else, switch)

Loops (for, while, do-while)

Pattern Problems (logic building)

Functions & Modular Programming

Arrays (1D & 2D)

Strings (Implementation & Problems)

Number System & Mathematics (GCD, Prime, Modular Arithmetic)

Time & Space Complexity (Big-O, Big-Theta, Big-Omega)

2. Data Structures & Algorithms (Problem Solving Mastery)
🔹 Linear DSA

Arrays & Strings (sliding window, prefix/suffix)

Number System & Maths (bit manipulation, modular arithmetic)

Binary Search & Variants

Two Pointers Technique

Recursion & Backtracking

Hashing (HashMap, Dictionary)

Sorting (Quick, Merge, Counting, Radix)

Linked List (SLL, DLL, Circular)

Stacks & Queues (Monotonic stack, Queue using stacks)

🔹 Non-Linear DSA

Trees (Traversal, LCA, Diameter)

Binary Trees & Binary Search Trees

Heaps & Priority Queues

Graphs (BFS, DFS, Dijkstra, Bellman-Ford, MST, Union-Find)

Greedy Algorithms

Dynamic Programming (Knapsack, LIS, DP on Trees)

🔹 Advanced DSA

Tries (Auto-complete, Dictionary Problems)

Segment Tree, Fenwick Tree

String Pattern Matching (KMP, Z, Rabin-Karp)

Advanced DP (Digit DP, DP with Bitmasking)

Advanced Graph Problems (Max Flow, Bridges, Articulation Points)

3. Computer Science Core Fundamentals

Operating Systems: Processes, Threads, Concurrency, Deadlocks, Scheduling, Memory Management

Computer Networks: OSI Model, TCP/IP, HTTP/HTTPS, DNS, Routing, Firewalls

DBMS:

SQL (DDL, DML, Joins, Triggers, Indexing)

NoSQL (MongoDB basics, Key-Value Stores)

Normalization, Transactions, ACID vs BASE

4. System Design
🔹 Low-Level Design (LLD)

Object-Oriented Programming (OOP in C#/Java)

SOLID Principles

Design Patterns (Singleton, Factory, Observer, Strategy, Repository, etc.)

UML Diagrams (Class, Sequence, Use Case)

Schema Design (SQL DBs)

API Design (REST, versioning, pagination, error handling)

Machine Coding Case Studies (BookMyShow, Splitwise, Tic-Tac-Toe)

🔹 High-Level Design (HLD)

Monolith vs Microservices

Distributed Systems Concepts

DNS, Load Balancing, Consistent Hashing

CAP Theorem, Caching (Redis, Memcached)

Content Delivery Networks (CDN)

SQL vs NoSQL Trade-offs

Messaging Queues (Kafka, RabbitMQ)

Scalability & Fault Tolerance

Security (JWT, OAuth, SSO, Encryption)

Case Studies (Design Netflix, WhatsApp, Uber, Amazon)

5. Full Stack .NET Development Specialization
🔹 Frontend Development (Angular/React)

HTML, CSS, JavaScript (Core + DOM + Events)

ES6+ (Async/Await, Modules, Fetch, Promises)

Angular (preferred for .NET ecosystem)

Components, Directives, Modules

Routing & Lazy Loading

Services & Dependency Injection

RxJS Observables

Forms (Template-driven, Reactive)

React (secondary option)

Functional Components & Hooks

React Router

State Management (Redux / Context API)

🔹 Backend Development (C#/.NET Core + Node.js optional)

C# Language Mastery

ASP.NET Core / .NET 8+

Controllers, Views, Models (MVC)

Dependency Injection

Middleware & Filters

REST API Development

Entity Framework Core (ORM)

Data Access Layer & Repository Pattern

Node.js (for microservices / side-projects)

Express.js basics

Middleware, Routing, JWT Authentication

🔹 Microservices & Architecture

Creating microservices with .NET & Spring Boot (Java optional)

Service Communication (REST, gRPC, Message Queues)

Database per service pattern

API Gateway (Ocelot, NGINX)

🔹 DevOps & Deployment

Git & GitHub (branching, PRs, workflows)

Docker & Containerization

CI/CD Pipelines (GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps, Jenkins)

Cloud Deployment on AWS / Azure

Security Best Practices (CSRF, XSS prevention, HTTPS, Secrets Management)

6. ML & AI for Software Developers

(Optional, but boosts career growth & relevance in 2025+)

Maths for ML (Linear Algebra, Probability, Statistics)

Machine Learning Basics (Regression, Classification, Clustering)

Neural Networks & Deep Learning Basics

Generative AI & Prompt Engineering

AI in Development (GitHub Copilot, AI-powered Code Review)

Projects:

Netflix User Engagement Prediction

AI-Powered Chatbot for Support

AI Code Optimization Tool

7. Placement & Career Preparation

Profile Building – Resume, LinkedIn, GitHub portfolio, LeetCode/Codeforces profile

DSA Revision – 200–300 curated problems across arrays, DP, graphs

CS Fundamentals Prep – OS, DBMS, CN, OOP

System Design – LLD & HLD practice case studies

Mock Interviews – Whiteboard + Online coding rounds

Job Applications – Target top product companies (Microsoft, Amazon, Google, Meta, Flipkart, Uber, etc.)

✅ With this roadmap, you’ll become a well-rounded Full Stack .NET Developer who is strong in:

DSA + CS fundamentals (for interviews)

System Design (for senior roles)

.NET Core + Angular/React Full Stack (for real-world development)

Cloud + Security + DevOps (for scalability)

AI/ML integration (for future-proofing career)
